        "geology": "Permo-triassic siltstone and sandstone",
        "hydrology": "The stream flow of the Huai Ma Nai catchment is seasonal.",
        "soils": "Soils are thin Alfisols and Ultisols with sandy clay loam to clayey texture, high coarse fragment content, low pH, high bulk density and low-medium cation exchange capacity",
        "vegetation": "Since the 1980s, deforestation and cultivation of cash crops expanded in this catchment supposed to be a ´protected forest´. Ethnic Thai farmers cultivated firstly soybean (Phaseolus aureusRoxb.) and mungbean (Glycine max. L. Merr.) untill 2002 and maize (Zea mays L.) since then. Land was cleared by slash-and-burn, followed by motorized ploughing and chemical weed control. Agricultural practices are very erosive generatign high levels of sediment yields (e.g. Valentin et al., 2008. AGEE; Huon et al., 2011; AGEE)."
      },
